      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\) and the fact that \\(x \\neq 1\\), we can express \\(x^{2017}\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x^{2017} = 2x - 1.\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Notice that this sum is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = 1\\) (since \\(x^0 = 1\\)) and the common ratio \\(r = x\\). The sum of a finite geometric series \\(a + ar + ar^2 + \\dots + ar^{n-1}\\) is given by \\(S_n = \\frac{a(r^n - 1)}{r - 1}\\).\n\nIn our case, the number of terms in the sum is 2017, so:\n\n\\[S_{2017} = \\frac{1 \\cdot (x^{2017} - 1)}{x - 1} = \\frac{(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
