      "text": "Let $P(x) = x^{2017} - 2x + 1.$  By the Factor Theorem, 165 divides the constant term, so the degree of the remainder is less than $n.$  Thus, by the Division Algorithm,\n\\[x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = (x - 1)(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1) + Q(x),\\]where the degree of $Q(x)$ is less than $2016.$  Evaluating at $x = 1,$ we get\n\\[P(1) = Q(1).\\]However, $Q(x) = -(x^{2017} - 2x + 1),$ so\n\\[P(1) = -(1^{2017} - 2 \\cdot 1 + 1) = 0.\\]Thus, $Q(1) = 0$ and $1$ is a root of $x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1,$ so \\[\nx^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 \\boxed{2 \\cdot 2^{2016}}.\\]. The answer is 2\\cdot2^{2016}",
