      "text": "We start with the given polynomial equation:\n\n\\[ x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0 \\]\n\nFirst, add 2x to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ x^{2017} + 2x - 2 = 0 \\]\n\nNow, we want to find the value of the sum of the series:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 \\]\n\nNotice that this series is a geometric series with the first term \\(a = x\\) and the common ratio \\(r = x\\), and it includes the term \\(x^0\\). The sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of a geometric series is given by:\n\n\\[ S_n = a \\frac{1 - r^n}{1 - r} \\]\n\nFor our series, \\(a = x\\), \\(r = x\\), and the number of terms is 2017 (since the series goes up to \\(x^{2017}\\)). So the sum of the series is:\n\n\\[ S_{2017} = x \\frac{1 - x^{2017}}{1 - x} \\]\n\nHowever, we can simplify this further because of the equation \\( x^{2017} + 2x - 2 = 0 \\). Rearrange this to express \\(x^{2017}\\) in terms of x:\n\n\\[ x^{2017} = 2 - 2x \\]\n\nNow substitute \\(x^{2017}\\) into the sum of the series:\n\n\\[ x \\frac{1 - (2 - 2x)}{1 - x} = x \\frac{1 - 2 + 2x}{1 - x} = x \\frac{2x - 1}{1 - x} = x(2x - 1) = 2x^2 - x \\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} = 2 - 2x\\), we know that:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} = x^2 \\cdot x^{2015} = x^2 \\cdot (2 - 2x) \\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = x^2 + (2 - 2x) + (2 - 2x) + \\dots + 2 - 2x + 2 = x^2 + (2(2017) - 2017(2x)) + 2 \\cdot 2017 \\]\n\nSimplify the constant term:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = x^2 + 4034 - 2017(2x) + 4034 = x^2 + 8068 - 4034x + 8068 = x^2 - 4034x + 16136 \\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} + 2x - 2 = 0\\), we get \\(x^{2016} - 2x + 2 = 0\\). Rearranging this:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} - 2x = -2 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\(-2\\) back into the expression:\n\n\\[ x^2 - 4034x + 16136 = 1 + (-2) = -1 + 8068 = 1 \\cdot \\frac{1 - 2x^{2017}}{1 - x} \\]\n\nSince \\(x^{2017} = 2 - 2x\\), we get:\n\n\\[ x^2 - 4034x = 2x^{2} - 4034x = 2 - 2x \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[ x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\boxed{1} \\]",
